== '''Overview''' ==

God, omnipotent and omniscient, had reached a state of boredom that would only be overcome if he committed suicide. For him, non-existence is superior to existence.

However, since suicide could only happen in time and space (an action only takes place within these conditions), God splits himself, creating Dialga and Palkia.
With the external conditions ensured for the decomposition process, there is now a missing entity that manifests God's will to cease: Arceus.

Arceus represents will-to-die and will exert its influence on the fact that everything is a finite process. However, in the initial fragmentation of God, another entity was created in addition to these 3: Giratina.
Giratina appears as a creation because God had a secondary objective to non-existence: to temporarily experience existence in an "imperfect" way.

In separate wills, each one would be a part of God, forgetting that they are part of God.

In these manifestations where Pokémon and human beings meet, Giratina is the force of life (or selfishness) that God created to fuel this temporary existence. Without a will-to-live, there would be no motivation to continue living.

The fragments of God over time only worried about death (which eventually always comes because the main and primordial purpose is non-existence).

Observing closely from the Distortion World, Giratina will oppose the acceleration of cosmic death, as he does not believe that the original God already wanted the total cessation of existence.


== '''Game plot''' ==
The game starts with the Protagonist arriving in Hessia. They got a new job in the research laboratory alongside Prof. George to study a phenomenon that is more common in Hessia than any other region, codename Zeta Program.

The Zeta Program has just one goal. To study Zeta Pokémon and find their secrets, especially what's causing them, where their power comes from, and why there are no physical differences between Zeta and non-Zeta Pokémon, which makes this endeavour even harder.

Prof. George leads this research alongside Prof. Arthur, his right-hand man. The Protagonist will join the team to search and capture new Zeta Pokémon, but their plans will suffer some changes due to the actions of Team Rebirth.

While unraveling the mysteries of Zeta Pokémon, the Protagonist will often question the actions of both their friends and foes and will have to take actions that can affect the course of the world.
